From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmt: drive the FM LNA only when the board describes one

The FM LNA hook (an ODM addition) reads the LNA pin from the CONSYS
node's pinctrl-4 and leaves fm_lna_pin_num at 0xffffffff when there is
none. wmt_func_fm_pre_ctrl() treats any non-zero pin number as "host
pin used for fm lna", so on a board without one every FM power-up and
power-down went to wmt_plat_fm_lna_ctrl(), which then failed to find
the fm_lna_state_* pin states and logged "Cannot find fm lna pin init
state!" as an error.

Start fm_lna_pin_num at 0, the "no pin" value its user checks for.
---
--- a/wmt_drv/common_main/platform/mtk_wcn_consys_hw.c
+++ b/wmt_drv/common_main/platform/mtk_wcn_consys_hw.c
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
 
 UINT32 gps_lna_pin_num = 0xffffffff;
 /* end ,prize-lifenfen-20181211, add FM_LNA_EN */
-UINT32 fm_lna_pin_num = 0xffffffff;
+UINT32 fm_lna_pin_num;
 /* begin ,prize-lifenfen-20181211, add FM_LNA_EN */
 
 INT32 chip_reset_status = -1;
